    pr_ref:  # d471
    description: "Filed 2026-05-21 after diagnosing WI-vuton's MessageBuilder case on chatwoot. The MessageBuilder case turned out to be a constructor-inheritance gap (now fixed in ruby.py — see commit 1ab55051fe), NOT a mixin gap. But the mixin gap is a separate real coverage hole in Ruby analysis that this item proposes to close.\n\n**The gap.**\n\nruby.py does not currently model include Module or extend Module for method resolution. When class A; include Foo; end is declared and A instances call a method defined on Foo, no calls or dispatches_to edge connects them in the behavior map. The Java analyzer's analog at java.py:1277-1461 does full inheritance-chain traversal with class_parents + up-to-10-level walking for inherited methods; Ruby has no equivalent.\n\n**Sample empirical impact.**\n\nCommon Rails patterns affected:\n- include Sidekiq::Worker — Sidekiq's perform_async, perform_in, set methods reached via include\n- include ActiveModel::Validations — validates, validate, errors methods\n- include Devise::Models::DatabaseAuthenticatable — Devise's password-management methods\n- Custom concerns under app/controllers/concerns/ and app/models/concerns/ — chatwoot has 36 concern symbols including AuthHelper, AttachmentConcern, etc.\n- ActiveSupport::Concern with included do blocks\n\nPer the 2026-05-21 cross-analyzer survey ('Survey ruby.py vs py.py call graph'): 'Ruby has no equivalent to Python's field type inference or Java's inheritance chain walking. Ruby passes 2 don't traverse include or extend declarations to link inherited methods.'\n\n**Architectural fit (per ADR-0003-ext).**\n\nBelongs in the Framework subcategory (per ADR-0003-ext §'Subcategory definitions'). Cousin of django_orm_dispatch.py / jackson_dispatch.py / airflow_framework_dispatch.py — framework-convention-specific dispatch recovery. Suggested module name: packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/linkers/ruby_mixin.py.\n\n**Design considerations for human review.**\n\n1. **Linker vs analyzer placement.** Existing Ruby Rails-callback emission (`_extract_rails_callbacks`) lives IN ruby.py, not in a linker. The 2026-05-21 design discussion concluded that the linker path is more architecturally clean for new work (consistent with Python/Java that defer most framework dispatch to linkers); the existing in-analyzer Rails callback emission can stay as precedent without expansion. Confirm this stance before implementing.\n\n2. **Edge type.** calls (with ast_call_inherited evidence_type, mirroring the constructor walk that just shipped) or dispatches_to (mirroring the type-hierarchy linker's polymorphic-override semantics)? Both have justification; pick one and document the choice in the linker's docstring.\n\n3. **Scope.** v1: explicit include ModuleName declarations where ModuleName resolves to a project symbol. v2 (defer): ActiveSupport::Concern with included do and class_methods do semantics. v3 (defer): refinement scopes (using Module).\n\n4. **Test coverage target.** Empty TestRailsModelCallbackEdges class exists at packages/hypergumbo-lang-mainstream/tests/test_ruby.py — extend it with mixin-resolution tests AND add a chatwoot-shaped mini-test (Sidekiq::Worker include or ActiveModel::Validations).\n\n5. **FP risk.** Many Ruby symbols share names across modules (e.g. `save`, `process`). Without rich name disambiguation, naive mixin walking could create FP edges. Suggest: require the included module to be a project symbol (skip gem modules), and emit at confidence 0.80-0.85 like the constructor walk.\n\n**Why needs_human_review (not todo_soft/todo_hard).**\n\nPer the AGENTS.md 'Creating a New Playbook' / governance rule for design judgment calls: linker placement choice (1) and edge type choice (2) are value judgments about architectural consistency that aren't structurally forced. They should be human-decided before agent implementation. The empirical value (Sidekiq workers, ActiveModel validations) is real but not WI-vuton-blocking; the constructor walk fix already shipped covers the chatwoot-specific reachability gap that motivated this investigation.\n\n**Cross-references.**\n- 1ab55051fe (this session's ruby constructor walk — the immediate predecessor)\n- WI-vuton (parent claim that originated the investigation)\n- ADR-0003-ext (Framework-subcategory linker convention)\n- java.py:1277-1461 (Java's class_parents inherited-method lookup — recipe)\n- ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/notebookjournal_05212026_1522.md (validation drain narrative)"  # d471
    fields: {}  # d471
