  message: "Cross-reference: new META INV-nilud filed today ('Inheritance-aware call resolution lives in linkers/inherited_calls.py, not in language analyzers') with 5-PR campaign plan at ~/puluf-plan.md (Alternative B). This item will close as part of WI-hatip (PR-2: linker substrate + Ruby migration), which lands the included_modules metadata extraction on ruby.py and the new includes edge type (emitted from extended inheritance.py). The architectural choice you flagged for human review — linker vs analyzer placement, edge type choice — is resolved as: (1) Tier-2 Infrastructure linker (cousin of inheritance.py, not Framework subcategory ruby_mixin.py as originally proposed); (2) new edge_type='includes' with evidence_type='ast_includes', emitted from extended inheritance.py rather than the new linker (because the structural relation is symmetric with extends/implements). Plan filed under META; this item stays needs_human_review until PR-2 merges and the substrate is in place."  # d593
